MGU Styles
==========

Custom instrument clusters for BMW iDrive 7: Toro, after the Lamborghini
Huracan, and M, BMW M's iDrive 8 M View rebuilt from a reference frame.
Source: https://github.com/waliworld/MGU-Styles

This package carries third-party work under its own licences:

* MGU App Kit (kit/), MIT licence, reproduced below.
  https://github.com/cauliflowermossgrape/idrive7-apps
  The copy here is the one vendored by ALMSTRA/idv7lol, which the MGU Store
  builds on the head unit.

* cluster_render_client.js, Mozilla Public License 2.0.
  Copyright (C) 2026 Robert Nisipeanu. Its source is the file itself and
  https://github.com/robertnisipeanu/idrive-apps (native/cluster-render/js).
  MPL-2.0 text: https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/

* The glyph atlas in atlas_data.js is baked from Saira, Chakra Petch,
  Michroma, Barlow Condensed, Barlow Semi Condensed and Inter Tight, SIL
  Open Font License 1.1, reproduced below. The M style's figures and
  symbols in it are drawn for this project (tools/mglyphs.py).

Measurements and signal decoding this work relies on, with thanks:
  the panel's bottom-strip rule, glass corners and telltale positions -
  Vizualyse/idrive-apps; the y=646 cut, the shader limits, the boost DIDs and
  the driving-mode and vehicle-state tables - ALMSTRA/idv7lol and the MGU
  App Kit; field scalings - ZEKAI-Design/ID7-Cluster-Themes.

The Huracan CORSA layout follows a reconstruction brief; the M layout is
traced from a photograph of a car's display, for the owner's own car. This
project has no connection with BMW AG or Automobili Lamborghini S.p.A.

